{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>They have laid it waste</b> — A thing decreed to be is spoken in the past tense." "<b>Into a ruin</b> — Like foam on the face of water, which has no substance to it." "<b>It has stripped it bare</b> — That it peeled it." "<b>Its branches have become white</b> — An intransitive verb, like הקיץ (\"he awoke\")."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:20.923736552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}